@anon.d1ff9934ece6813bf2a30f9ce237ed68.2434 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [665 x i8] }> <{ [665 x i8] c"# `coverage_attribute`\0A\0AThe tracking issue for this feature is: [#84605]\0A\0A[#84605]: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/84605\0A\0A---\0A\0AThe `coverage` attribute can be used to selectively disable coverage\0Ainstrumentation in an annotated function. This might be useful to:\0A\0A-   Avoid instrumentation overhead in a performance critical function\0A-   Avoid generating coverage for a function that is not meant to be executed,\0A    but still target 100% coverage for the rest of the program.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```rust\0A#![feature(coverage_attribute)]\0A\0A// `foo()` will get coverage instrumentation (by default)\0Afn foo() {\0A  // ...\0A}\0A\0A#[coverage(off)]\0Afn bar() {\0A  // ...\0A}\0A```\0A" }>, align 1
