@anon.d1ff9934ece6813bf2a30f9ce237ed68.3165 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [677 x i8] }> <{ [677 x i8] c"# `try_blocks`\0A\0AThe tracking issue for this feature is: [#31436]\0A\0A[#31436]: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/31436\0A\0A------------------------\0A\0AThe `try_blocks` feature adds support for `try` blocks. A `try`\0Ablock creates a new scope one can use the `?` operator in.\0A\0A```rust,edition2018\0A#![feature(try_blocks)]\0A\0Ause std::num::ParseIntError;\0A\0Alet result: Result<i32, ParseIntError> = try {\0A    \221\22.parse::<i32>()?\0A        + \222\22.parse::<i32>()?\0A        + \223\22.parse::<i32>()?\0A};\0Aassert_eq!(result, Ok(6));\0A\0Alet result: Result<i32, ParseIntError> = try {\0A    \221\22.parse::<i32>()?\0A        + \22foo\22.parse::<i32>()?\0A        + \223\22.parse::<i32>()?\0A};\0Aassert!(result.is_err());\0A```\0A" }>, align 1
