@anon.d1ff9934ece6813bf2a30f9ce237ed68.3223 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [788 x i8] }> <{ [788 x i8] c"# `unsized_tuple_coercion`\0A\0AThe tracking issue for this feature is: [#42877]\0A\0A[#42877]: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/42877\0A\0A------------------------\0A\0AThis is a part of [RFC0401]. According to the RFC, there should be an implementation like this:\0A\0A```rust,ignore (partial-example)\0Aimpl<..., T, U: ?Sized> Unsized<(..., U)> for (..., T) where T: Unsized<U> {}\0A```\0A\0AThis implementation is currently gated behind `#[feature(unsized_tuple_coercion)]` to avoid insta-stability. Therefore you can use it like this:\0A\0A```rust\0A#![feature(unsized_tuple_coercion)]\0A\0Afn main() {\0A    let x : ([i32; 3], [i32; 3]) = ([1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6]);\0A    let y : &([i32; 3], [i32]) = &x;\0A    assert_eq!(y.1[0], 4);\0A}\0A```\0A\0A[RFC0401]: https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/blob/master/text/0401-coercions.md\0A" }>, align 1
